# Line endings. `.editorconfig` already says `end_of_line = lf`, but that binds
# editors, not `git checkout` — and Git for Windows defaults to
# `core.autocrlf=true`, so a clone there rewrites every text file to CRLF
# before any editor sees it. That is not cosmetic here: `scripts/retry.sh` is
# copied into the image and run during the build (`Dockerfile:23,28`), and a
# shebang ending in `\r` makes `docker compose up` fail on the very first
# build — the path this project recommends to Windows users. `Makefile` needs
# LF too. The tree is text through and through; `text=auto` still detects and
# leaves alone anything binary added later.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Two branches that each add an entry are not in conflict: keep both. This
# only helps a local merge or rebase (GitHub's merge check ignores it) and is
# a fallback now that entries go in changelog.d/ — see changelog.d/README.md.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
